# The two marks a toggle draws for itself: a checkbox's tick and a switch's
# thumb, each one off and on, at every size, colour and box shape that changes
# them.
#
# A picture per `ToggleKind`, and a band per thing that moves the mark. Every
# band holds the same toggle twice — bound to `false`, then to `true` — so off
# and on are side by side and the difference between them is the whole subject.
# That is what a snapshot of a toggle could not say before: the box changed
# colour and nothing else, so a switch was a small filled bar and a ticked
# checkbox was a filled square with no check in it.
#
# The mark follows the **signal**, because that is what a browser reads: an
# `<input type=checkbox>` is `:checked` when its `checked` property is set, and
# the property is the signal. The mark is drawn by the widget in all three
# renderers — the sheet's `::before` on a page, `mark:tick` and `mark:thumb` in
# the scene document, and a stroke and a disc in the painter — so a program can
# neither ask for a mark that does not exist nor leave a toggle without one.
#
# The `On(.Checked)` bands read right now that buri#119 has closed: the `on`
# cell of each carries its checked palette and the `off` cell beside it does
# not, because `describe` reads the toggle's own signal rather than the state
# the snapshot was asked for. The same signal moves the mark, so the fill and
# the mark cannot come apart.
#
# Beside every picture is a `describe` assertion naming what the scene carries,
# which is what says a mark is in the document and not only in the pixels: a
# checkbox has `mark:tick` when it is on and nothing when it is off, and a
# switch has `mark:thumb` either way with the alignment that moves it.
#
# The lifecycle is the sweeps': every golden compares, a renamed snapshot is
# reported as missing rather than as a difference, `--update` records it, the
# run after that compares against what it wrote, and an edit that moves one
# number fails the comparison.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "the tick a checkbox draws and the thumb a switch moves, each off and on across size, colour and box shape, as 2 pictures with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/marks", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/marks/test/__snapshots__/toggle-checkbox.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet is reported as missing, with the command
# that records one, rather than as a difference against nothing.
edit {
  file: "lib/marks/test/pictures.buri"
  replace: "\"toggle-checkbox\""
  with: "\"never-recorded\""
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/marks", "--force", "--filter=tick"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/marks/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/marks", "--update", "--force", "--filter=tick"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/marks/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/marks", "--force", "--filter=tick"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# The negative twin: three more pixels of padding on the switch's track, which
# moves every thumb in that picture and nothing in the other one.
edit {
  file: "lib/marks/scenes.buri"
  replace: ".Padding(.Px(2))"
  with: ".Padding(.Px(5))"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/marks", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/marks/test/__snapshots__/toggle-switch.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/marks/test/__snapshots__/toggle-checkbox.diff.png"  exists: false }
